# Powers the GitHub Activity graph. Used on the server only, never sent to visitors.
# Create a classic token with NO scopes at https://github.com/settings/tokens/new —
# it can only read public data, which is all the graph needs.
# Private contributions appear as plain counts once "Private contributions" is
# switched on in your GitHub profile's contribution settings.
# In local development the site falls back to your GitHub CLI login (`gh auth token`).
GITHUB_TOKEN=
